ey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e9317f868ac54b27421f61d2ffc42400b73140ae9e337a05b6567be56a8a6a23","event_uuid":"2deead57-2f0f-46f0-bd96-0d30381e008c","position":{"commit_sha":"3bfaf278025c38b2bb2ca9e29620a97e3020addd","position":"1785012884447740879-2deead57-2f0f-46f0-bd96-0d30381e008c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-219_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"129c3e1b-fbb8-4415-b42d-694fe0d70419","comments":[],"created_at":1784952017321898001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"855ac0fe-b9c3-4465-952b-70bb699633f1","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"72d9-8fbd-3a9e-48a6"},{"link_uuid":"d2810809-eda7-4753-97e2-a4b4c848d171","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5128-0856-d80f-4eb6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nA container ticket (epic/story with children) rarely declares its own `file_impact`, so its\nplan-review attestation's signed dependency set is empty and the code-drift gate falls back to\nwhole-HEAD invalidation (ADR 0002 decision 5): ANY commit — however unrelated — invalidates the\ncontainer's attestation, forcing a re-review or drift-refresh on every merge. This is the\ncontainer-scale form of the over-invalidation ADR 0002 was written to fix, and a real\ngate-economics drag under the parallel epic/child workflow where the base ref moves constantly.\n\nThe scope a container plan actually reasons about is its children's declared scope. The\ninvalidation lattice for inheritance already exists: `material_fingerprint` (pass1.py:551)\nhashes a ticket's description + file_impact + child ids, and a container review pins each\nDIRECT child's material fingerprint into the signed manifest — so a child editing its\nfile_impact (or a child being added/removed) already invalidates the container's attestation\nvia pin/material drift, forcing a re-review that recomputes any inherited union. Inheritance\ntherefore cannot go silently stale one level deep. It does NOT hold for grandchildren (a\nchild's fingerprint covers grandchild IDS only, not grandchild file_impact), which is why\ninheritance is DIRECT CHILDREN ONLY — deeper drift is covered by the deeper tickets' own\nattestations, mirroring the review model (reviews pin direct dependencies; dependency-order\nreview covers each tier).\n\nDepends on 72d9-8fbd (athletic-esthetical-polecat) landing first: before that fix, scoped\ndependency sets are inert in attested mode, so giving containers a non-empty set would move\nthem OFF the only working invalidation (whole-HEAD) onto a broken path.\n\n## Approach\n1. In `dependency_hashes` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py): when the reviewed ticket\n   has children, compute the candidate union = own `file_impact` ∪ review citations ∪ the\n   union of DIRECT children's `file_impact`. Apply the POISON RULE: if any non-closed direct\n   child has an empty `file_impact`, do NOT inherit — keep the pre-change set (own ∪\n   citations; empty ⇒ whole-HEAD fallback), preserving fail-closed for undeclared scope.\n   Closed children neither contribute files nor poison (their work is delivered; ADR 0024's\n   completion floor deliberately stops re-litigating it, and their files' later churn belongs\n   to other tickets). NO new store reads: the orchestrator already fetches every direct\n   child whole (`orchestrator.assemble_context` -> `ctx.children`, each carrying status and\n   file_impact), so thread that list through as an optional parameter —\n   `_run_plan_review` passes `ctx.children` to `attest.sign_plan_review(children=...)`,\n   which forwards to `dependency_hashes(children=...)` (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py\n   and attest.py gain the threading; manifest.py consumes it). This also avoids any\n   tickets-root ambiguity in attested mode (the child states were read from the pinned\n   ticket snapshot by the same review run). `children=None` (default — e.g. the resign\n   recovery path, which has no assembled context) means NO inheritance: the dep set stays\n   the pre-change own-impact ∪ citations, which is the conservative direction (an empty set\n   falls back to whole-HEAD invalidation), and the drift-refresh path re-hashes the PRIOR\n   signed dep set so an inherited scope survives refresh unchanged.\n2. Extend P9 (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py, `p9_file_impact_coverage`): containers\n   currently auto-pass. Keep passing when inheritance is effective (every non-closed direct\n   child declares file_impact, and there is at least one). Surface an ADVISORY (never\n   blocking) on a container whose inheritance is poisoned, naming the children with empty\n   file_impact, so authors see exactly why the epic stays on whole-HEAD invalidation. Leaf\n   behavior unchanged.\n3. Document: docs/plan-review-gate.md (scoped-drift paragraph: containers inherit direct\n   children's declared impact under the poison rule) and a short amendment note in\n   docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md decision 5.\nRejected: recursive (whole-subtree) inheritance — the pin lattice only self-heals one level\ndeep, so a grandchild file_impact edit would leave a recursively-computed union silently\nstale. Rejected: inheriting a partial union when some children lack file_impact — that flips\nthe empty-set fallback from fail-closed to fail-open for exactly the undeclared portion.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py (dependency_hashes + a small child-union helper)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py and src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py (thread\n  ctx.children through sign_plan_review into dependency_hashes; no new store reads)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py (P9 container extension)\n- tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review.py (the existing P9 unit tests pin the old container auto-pass\n  and must be updated to the new container semantics)\n- docs/plan-review-gate.md, docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md\n\n## Testing\nInterface tests in tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py against a tmp repo with\nthe suite's attested/ref=HEAD default, committing drift via the existing `_commit_all` helper:\ncontainer+children fixtures asserting the signed manifest's `dep` paths (inherited union,\npoison rule, closed-child exclusion), claim-gate outcomes (unrelated commit keeps the claim\nopen; a committed change to a child-declared file blocks the claim naming drift), the\nchild-file_impact-edit → container pin invalidation property, and DET-floor unit assertions\nfor the P9 container advisory. In tests/unit/test_plan_review.py, replace\ntest_p9_not_applicable_for_container (which asserts the old unconditional container pass)\nwith three container cases: effective inheritance passes, a non-closed impact-less child\nyields the poisoning advisory naming the child id, and a closed impact-less child does not\npoison; leaf cases unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A container whose non-closed direct children all declare non-empty file_impact signs a\n      dependency set equal to own file_impact ∪ citations ∪ the children's union — asserted\n      by parsing `dep` lines from the signed manifest in an interface test.\n- [ ] Poison rule: if any non-closed direct child has empty file_impact, the signed set is\n      unchanged from pre-change behavior (empty ⇒ whole-HEAD fallback applies) — asserted by\n      manifest inspection plus a claim blocked after an unrelated commit.\n- [ ] Closed children neither contribute paths nor poison the union — asserted with a fixture\n      containing one closed impact-less child.\n- [ ] With inheritance effective: an unrelated committed change does NOT invalidate the\n      container attestation (claim succeeds); a committed change to a child-declared file\n      DOES (claim blocked, reason names drift) — both asserted via rebar.claim.\n- [ ] A child editing its file_impact after the container review invalidates the container's\n      attestation (pin/material drift) — asserted via claim_gate_check.\n- [ ] P9: a container with poisoned inheritance yields an advisory naming the offending\n      child id(s); a container with effective inheritance passes; leaf behavior is unchanged —\n      asserted in DET-floor tests.\n- [ ] docs/plan-review-gate.md and ADR 0002 describe container inheritance and the poison\n      rule.\n- [ ] make lint, make typecheck, and the default non-integration pytest suite exit zero.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py","reason":"dependency_hashes child-union inheritance + poison rule"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"thread children into sign_plan_review"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"pass ctx.children at the sign site"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py","reason":"P9 container advisory"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py","reason":"interface tests for inheritance/poison/claim outcomes"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review.py","reason":"migrate P9 container unit tests to the new semantics"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document container inheritance"},{"path":"docs/adr/0002-code-drift-invalidation.md","reason":"decision-5 amendment note"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","5128-0856-d80f-4eb6"],["depends_on","72d9-8fbd-3a9e-48a6"]],"parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"614e1313-88fb-4a3d-9827-fc8d766f36c6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3e4b-c9f5-490b-4531","ticket_type":"task","title":"Container plan-review drift scope inherits direct children's file_impact","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["437d64ce-ab9a-4018-bc29-9df49b9ee70e","855ac0fe-b9c3-4465-952b-70bb699633f1","d2810809-eda7-4753-97e2-a4b4c848d171","baf06db6-c180-421b-bc20-9ed61ed32a07","a56590a8-af92-47d8-a0df-0bd35e8f0161","6ebb5835-4cec-4773-8490-50af98c39b00","f2c153ec-2028-4e25-bd6c-82614cf9f15e","bebe805c-5092-42ee-9d45-b20821f2ac11","614e1313-88fb-4a3d-9827-fc8d766f36c6","d00ed5ea-64d6-4143-8750-89d7fc0a188a","2deead57-2f0f-46f0-bd96-0d30381e008c"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785012884447740880,"uuid":"c01761c1-f5ee-4a18-98b2-b1dcea3711aa"}